1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Ten STL designs. Eleven printed parts.
Bronze Dalek | Original TTGO T-Display ESP32 | CAD assembly preview

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:13,000
01 | Reinforced motor base
Mate four Adafruit 3777 motors with 3766 wheels; lower the pairs into the one-piece base.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:19,000
02 | Retain the motors
Eight padded clamp strips and sixteen M3 bolts retain the four motors.

4
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:25,000
03 | Lower skirt first
Fasten the lower ring to the base before fitting electronics; seat its locating joint.

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:36,000
04 | Electronics and battery
Fit two FR4 plates, nylon spacers and boards; secure the disconnected 12 V, 6 Ah battery with two straps.

6
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:41,000
05 | Stack the upper skirt
Seat the complete upper skirt and fasten its four M4 joints.

7
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:51,000
06 | Fit the shoulder components
Bench fit speaker, rear T-Display, four edge-retaining tabs and both power switches.

8
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:57,000
07 | Seat the shoulder
Connect labelled harness plugs, leave service loops and fasten the shoulder.

9
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:04,000
08 | Fasten the neck
Tighten the neck bolts before fitting the head drive servo.

10
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:13,000
09 | Bearing-supported head
Fit two 608 bearings, retainers, inner-race spacer, narrow shims and M8 spindle. Keep the head loose for belt fitting.

11
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:20,000
10 | Head drive
Fit the FS5103R and pulley. Preload the O-ring on the loose head hub, then lower and retain the head.

12
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:29,000
11 | Two-axis arm assemblies
Fit two yaw servos, two shared carriers, two pitch servos and both arms; centre horns before attachment.

13
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:36,000
12 | Local Wi-Fi control
Illustrative rear screen: direct access point, then access point plus a 2.4 GHz network.

14
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:44,000
13 | Head and arm motion
Simulated continuous head rotation and circular arm-tip paths. Original robot sound effects.

15
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:55,000
14 | Four-wheel motion
Simulated forward travel, broad moving arc, reverse and stop on a level floor.

16
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Assembly complete | Prototype design
543.8 mm tall | Physical fit, strength, driving and stop tests remain required. See the assembly manual.
